The paired fusion-vs-32f difference is − 0.27 -0.27 points over 1,132 observations on 581 distinct questions, with
question-clustered standard errors giving a 90% CI of [ − 2.09 , + 1.56 ] [-2.09,+1.56] points;
two one-sided tests reject differences larger than the pre-registered ± 2.5 \pm 2.5 -point margin at p = .022 p{=}.022 . On the union control the shared logit path clears the same margin per model ( p = .035 p{=}.035 / .046 .046 , “Same-pipeline replication” above).

